<title>USA: Pepsi-Cola Puerto Rico sued by shareholders.</title>
<headline>Pepsi-Cola Puerto Rico sued by shareholders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A class action lawsuit has been filed by a group of shareholders against Pepsi-Cola Puerto Rico Bottling Co, two law firms said Monday.</p>
<p>The law firms, Vincente &amp; Cuebas, and Nachman Santiago &amp; Guillemard of San Juan, Puerto Rico, said the company violated federal securities laws by misrepresenting or making material omissions about its financial condition between September 19, 1995 and August 15, 1996.</p>
<p>The lawsuit seeks to recover damages on behalf of all purchasers of the company's Class B common stock between those dates.</p>
